    "body": "## Result\n\nThis PR studies the complete 112-dimensional normalized A4 source under two-sided conjugation by `I+t^-1 N`, where the credited source slice N has rank 16 and N²=0. It allows arbitrary constant rank-110 input/output compressions and arbitrary Laurent first maps.\n\nThe full saturated limit L acts by scalars on a fixed 12-dimensional subspace. Compression can recover directions after killing leading coefficients, but it recovers at most the number lost. A full M(10,10,11) target therefore requires at least nine lost directions: `dim(P L C) <= 103`.\n\nThe structural continuation proves that every element of L of ordinary rank at most four lies entirely in its bottom-left 28-by-28 block. That block is the explicit 46-dimensional space `E = G + [G,F] + F G F`, with F=G00. Consequently a successful arbitrary constant compression requires rank-26 outer maps with `dim(Phat E Chat) <= 37`. This is a necessary condition; arbitrary noncoordinate compressions remain open.\n\n## Complete coordinate exclusions\n\nThe original census checks all 6,216 principal two-coordinate deletions of L. Every projected dimension is at least 108 over C, so none meets the nine-direction requirement.\n\nThe latest continuation covers all **142,884 independent two-row / two-column deletions** of E. Modular ranks at 1009 give complex lower bounds with histogram:\n\n| Dimension modulo 1009 | Pairs |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 40 | 2 |\n| 41 | 59 |\n| 42 | 1,482 |\n| 43 | 2,168 |\n| 44 | 19,151 |\n| 45 | 15,096 |\n| 46 | 104,926 |\n\nTwo exact integer six-dimensional kernel witnesses attain dimension 40. Thus every independent coordinate compression of the complete fixed family loses at most six directions, and the entire coordinate class is excluded. This does not classify arbitrary complex flags.\n\n## Completed principal-pair explorations\n\nTwo further specified singular paths retain every source slice:\n\n| Path | Principal pairs | Exact re-saturations | Survivors |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Two noncommuting square-zero factors | 6,216 | 0 | 0 |\n| Moving unit from their nonnilpotent sum | 6,216 | 221 | 0 |\n\nAll 221 re-saturations have complete rational polynomial replay and an exact invariant-subspace obstruction. The note also proves `ell >= 10*ceil((s-2)/11)-1`, giving required loss 29 for the first path's 29-dimensional scalar-action subspace.\n\n## Validation\n\nReviewed head: `3b2eb05abac534da201b4ec411e914182cb46b8a`.\nReviewed tree: `35090c7ceee3a22d30f20f34ae7989d71fb9b6d8`.\n\n- All 15 package tests passed: eight original conjugation tests, three block-reduction tests, and four independent-coordinate tests.\n- Nine repository metadata and archive checks passed. Source pins also passed within the package tests.\n- The complete independent-coordinate census and both sharpness witnesses replayed successfully. Both exploratory reports reproduced byte-identically, including all 221 exact re-saturations.\n- Historical full-regression evidence covers 905 unique test IDs at frozen tree `363271b34a2b82dd033b388d7b48d00f1e76d1f9`. Its disclosed scratch-link failure and successful correction are retained. This is not a fresh full-suite run on the current tree.\n- All 295 claims from main remain unchanged. Existing implementations, tests, and archive bytes are preserved.\n\nRequired hosted CI must pass before merge.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nThe four claims—`AI-A4-TWOSIDED-RANKLOSS-001`, `AI-A4-TWOSIDED-COORDINATE-002`, `AI-A4-TWOSIDED-LOWRANK-003`, and `AI-A4-INDEPENDENT-COORDINATE-004`—remain `proof-written-unreviewed`.\n\nThe original tensor, normalization, source slice, and minimum-rank theorem retain their existing attribution and exact pins. Arbitrary noncoordinate compressions, moving compressions, and other singular paths remain open. No full target, exponent improvement, historical priority, formalization, or independent mathematical review is claimed. Root and sibling-agent checks belong to the same generating session.\n",
